File: zebra.info,  Node: Top,  Next: Overview,  Prev: (dir),  Up: (dir)

Zebra
*****

   Zebra is a multi-server routing software package which provides
TCP/IP based routing protocols such as RIPv1, RIPv2, OSPFv2, OSPFv3,
BGP-4, BGP-4+ and so on.  Zebra turns your machine into a full powered
router.

   This is the Zebra Manual for zebra-0.73.

   This manual describes `zebra' and some other beasts.

* Menu:

* Overview::                    Overview of the Zebra world.
* Installation::                How to install Zebra.
* Configuration File::          Configuration file description.
* VTY::                         Virtual terminal interface.

Zebra beasts
* zebra::                       Routing manager daemon.
* ripd::                        RIPv2,RIPv1 protocol daemon.
* ripngd::                      RIPng protocol daemon.
* ospfd::                       OSPFv2 protocol daemon.
* ospf6d::                      OSPFv3 protocol daemon.
* bgpd::                        BGP-4,BGP-4+ protocol daemon.

Advanced Features
* Filtering::                   How to filter routes.
* Route map::                   Route map description.
* IPv6 supports::               IP version 6 supports.
* Kernel interface::            Zebra between kernel interface.
* Linux netlink::               Netlink mechanism on Linux box.
* Zebra protocol::              Zebra protocol.

Copying
* Copying::                     The GNU General Public License.

